DP  - 2026 Mar
TI  - Pre-Transplant Infection Screening and Vaccination During Prolonged Waiting 
      Periods for Lung Transplantation in Donor-Limited Asia-Pacific Settings.
PG  - 232-235
LID - 10.1002/resp.70226 [doi]
AB  - Donor limitation and prolonged waiting period create a need for time‐based 
      infection screening and vaccination in lung transplant candidates. Respiratory 
      cultures at listing are insufficient without repeat cultures and updated 
      susceptibilities during the waiting period. Perioperative antimicrobials for 
      multidrug‐resistant gram‐negative rods, moulds, and nontuberculous mycobacteria 
      should be prepared in advance of organ allocation. Vaccination should be 
      completed early during the waiting period; live vaccines should be given before 
      transplantation only when indicated and eligible.
