TI  - Contemporary Concise Review 2021: Interstitial lung disease.
PG  - 539-548
LID - 10.1111/resp.14278 [doi]
AB  - The last 2 years have presented previously unforeseen challenges in pulmonary 
      medicine. Despite the significant impact of the SARS-CoV-2 pandemic on patients, 
      clinicians and communities, advances in the care and understanding of 
      interstitial lung disease (ILD) continued unabated. Recent studies have led to 
      improved guidelines, better understanding of the role for antifibrotics in 
      fibrosing ILDs, prognostic indicators and novel biomarkers. In this concise 
      contemporary review, we summarize many of the important studies published in 
      2021, highlighting their relevance and impact to the management and knowledge of 
      ILD.
