TI  - Training in interventional pulmonology: What we have learned and a way forward.
PG  - 997-1007
LID - 10.1111/resp.13846 [doi]
AB  - IP encompasses a complex list of procedures requiring knowledge, technical skills 
      and competence. Modern, learner-centric educational philosophies and an explosion 
      of multidimensional educational tools including manikins, simulators, online 
      resources, social media and formal programs can foster learning in IP, promoting 
      professionalism and a culture of lifelong learning. This paper provides 
      background and guidance to a structured, multidimensional and learner-centric 
      strategy for medical procedural education. Focusing on our experience in IP, we 
      describe how competency-based measures, simulation technology and various 
      teaching modalities contribute to a more uniform learning environment in which 
      patients do not suffer the burdens of procedure-related training.
