TI  - Add-on interventions during pulmonary rehabilitation.
PG  - 899-908
LID - 10.1111/resp.13585 [doi]
AB  - Both pulmonary rehabilitation (PR) and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease 
      (COPD) are generic terms and it increasingly becomes clear that rehabilitation 
      programmes need to be tailored to the complexity and circumstances of the 
      individual patient. Indeed, PR is described as a comprehensive, individualized 
      intervention based on thorough assessment of identifiable treatable traits. The 
      current review summarizes ongoing developments regarding additional interventions 
      and tools to facilitate PR and improve outcomes in patients with a chronic 
      respiratory disease.
