TI  - Thoracic Society of Australia and New Zealand oxygen guidelines for acute oxygen 
      use in adults: 'Swimming between the flags'.
PG  - 1182-91
LID - 10.1111/resp.12620 [doi]
AB  - The purpose of the Thoracic Society of Australia and New Zealand guidelines is to 
      provide simple, practical evidence-based recommendations for the acute use of 
      oxygen in adults in clinical practice. The intended users are all health 
      professionals responsible for the administration and/or monitoring of oxygen 
      therapy in the management of acute medical patients in the community and hospital 
      settings (excluding perioperative and intensive care patients), those responsible 
      for the training of such health professionals, and both public and private health 
      care organizations that deliver oxygen therapy.
