TI  - Pleuroparenchymal fibroelastosis in association with carcinomas.
PG  - 191-4
LID - 10.1111/resp.12654 [doi]
AB  - PPFE is a rare disease characterized by upper lobe pleural fibrosis and 
      parenchymal fibroelastosis. Its aetiology is considered idiopathic, although 
      possible causative factors have been described. An association of PPFE with solid 
      tumours is unknown and has not been considered previously. We identified six 
      patients with PPFE, four of them with a coexisting malignancy. The case series 
      suggests that PPFE might be an implication of varying factors rather than being 
      an exclusively idiopathic condition.
