TI  - Asthma research in China: a five-year review.
PG  - 10-9
LID - 10.1111/resp.12196 [doi]
AB  - Asthma is one of the most common chronic diseases worldwide with increasing 
      morbidity. China has the largest asthmatic population and is one of the countries 
      with the highest asthma mortality. Fortunately, asthma research in China, both 
      clinical and scientific, has developed markedly over the past few years. This has 
      resulted in significant increases in our understanding of Chinese asthma 
      prevalence, risk factors, control status, pathogenesis, and new prevention or 
      treatment strategies. In this review, the major achievements of asthma research 
      in China from 2008 to 2012 are summarized.
