TI  - Pneumococci: immunology of the innate host response.
PG  - 1057-63
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2010.01814.x [doi]
AB  - Despite the development of vaccines and antibiotics, Streptococcus pneumoniae 
      (the pneumococcus) continues to be a major cause of human morbidity and mortality 
      throughout the world. In recent years our understanding of how the host innate 
      immune system recognizes and responds to pneumococcal infection has advanced 
      significantly. Herein, we highlight some of the key features of the innate 
      response to the pneumococcus.
