TI  - Strategies for non-responders.
PG  - S41-3
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2009.01575.x [doi]
AB  - When improvements in symptoms of hospital-acquired pneumonia are difficult to 
      see, an investigation should be made into whether there truly is no response to 
      antimicrobial treatment. Non-infectious disease that results in pneumonia-like 
      shadows needs to be excluded. In pneumonia that is unresponsive to 
      antimicrobials, differential diagnoses must be made with consideration of 
      causative microorganism factors, host factors and medication factors, 
      respectively. Preferably, the dose, administration frequency and administration 
      time for the administered antimicrobials should be established based on PK/PD.
