TI  - Prostatic metastasis of large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of the lung.
PG  - 772-5
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2009.01545.x [doi]
AB  - Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma (LCNEC) of the lung is a rare and aggressive 
      tumour with a poor prognosis. Lung cancer metastases to the prostate are also 
      uncommon, and are usually found incidentally during autopsy. Most reported 
      primary lung cancers with prostatic metastases are small cell carcinomas, and 
      prostatic metastases from LCNEC of the lung have not been reported previously. 
      This case report describes a 70-year-old man with LCNEC of the lung and 
      metastases in the prostate, brain, bone, liver and lymph nodes.
