TI  - Update on influenza anti-virals.
PG  - S19-21
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2008.01249.x [doi]
AB  - While the mainstay of prevention and control of any viral infection has 
      historically been the use of vaccines, it is recognized that the pace of a global 
      pandemic is likely to be such that it is unlikely that an effective vaccine will 
      be ready for the first wave of an influenza pandemic. As such, in addition to 
      non-pharmacological public health and infection control measures, the first line 
      of action will be the use of antivirals.
