TI  - Cyclophosphamide-induced acute respiratory distress syndrome.
PG  - 769-73
AB  - Cyclophosphamide is widely used in neoplastic and inflammatory diseases. Although 
      several adverse events have been described with its use, acute and subacute 
      interstitial pneumonitis leading to pulmonary fibrosis is rare and potentially 
      fatal. This case report describes a 64-year-old man who, after the fifth 
      chemotherapy cycle, developed a severe ARDS leading to pulmonary fibrosis in just 
      30 days.
