TI  - Hydatid cyst presenting as an eosinophilic pleural effusion.
PG  - 462-4
AB  - A 61-year-old woman presented with an eosinophilic pleural effusion, secondary to 
      transdiaphragmatic intrapleural spread of an hepatic hydatid cyst. Right 
      posterolateral thoracotomy and frenotomy revealed a loculated pleural effusion 
      associated with a 10 x 8 cm hydatid cyst in the posterior segment of the liver. 
      Hydatid disease should be included in the differential diagnosis of eosinophilic 
      pleural effusions in endemic regions.
