TI  - Recombinant factor VIIa treatment for life-threatening haemoptysis.
PG  - 652-4
AB  - Diffuse alveolar haemorrhage is a severe clinical disorder that may be 
      life-threatening. The early diagnosis of diffuse alveolar haemorrhage and prompt 
      intervention is crucial. Recombinant factor VIIa has been used extensively for 
      the treatment of haemophilia A and B patients. More recently, recombinant factor 
      VIIa has been used successfully for the treatment of bleeding in patients without 
      pre-existing coagulopathy. We describe the successful use of recombinant factor 
      VIIa in a patient with diffuse alveolar haemorrhage secondary to pulmonary-renal 
      syndrome.
