TI  - Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma presenting as a unilateral solitary round pulmonary 
      hilar node infarction.
PG  - 224-6
AB  - Unilateral solitary pulmonary hilar node adenopathy is a rare presentation of 
      diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. In this report, the authors present a case with a 
      solitary pulmonary hilar lymph node infarction caused by diffuse large B-cell 
      lymphoma. Enhanced CT examinations revealed a well-defined round mass with 
      homogenous low attenuation in the left pulmonary hilum. Both radiological imaging 
      and pathological examination can provide useful information for the 
      interpretation of abnormalities and may enable the diagnosis of rare aetiologies.
