TI  - Pulmonary cryptococcosis: a case report and review of the Asian-Pacific 
      experience.
PG  - 351-5
AB  - Pulmonary cryptococcosis is a very rare form of pneumonia, which is seldom seen 
      among immunocompetent patients. We report the case of a 36-year-old man who 
      presented with indolent pneumonia that was subsequently diagnosed to be pulmonary 
      cryptococcosis without other systemic involvement. Contrary to formal belief, 
      there was evidence of residual lung fibrosis 12 months after initial 
      presentation. The features of pulmonary cryptococcosis reported in the Asian 
      Pacific region are also reviewed.
