TI  - Lemierre's syndrome.
PG  - 171-3
AB  - This is a case report of Lemierre's syndrome in a 17-year-old male patient. 
      Lemierre's disease consists of suppurative thrombophlebitis of the internal 
      jugular vein (SIJVT) in the presence of oropharyngeal infection and can be 
      complicated by septic pulmonary embolism. Other causes of SIJVT include deep neck 
      infections and central venous catheterization. The disease usually results from 
      Gram-negative anaerobic organisms such as Fusobacterium necrophorum.
