IS  - 1323-7799 (Linking)
VI  - 25
IP  - 9
DP  - 2020 Sep
TI  - Bronchoscopic interventions for severe emphysema: Where are we now?
PG  - 972-980
LID - 10.1111/resp.13835 [doi]
AB  - Patients with severe emphysema have limited treatment options and only derive a 
      small benefit from optimal medical treatment. The only other therapy to have 
      significant clinical beneficial effect in emphysema is LVRS but the perceived 
      risk and invasiveness of surgery has fuelled bronchoscopic approaches to induce 
      lung volume reduction. There are multiple bronchoscopic methods for achieving 
      volume reduction in severe emphysema: EBV, airway bypass procedure, endobronchial 
      coils, thermal (vapour) sclerosis and chemical sclerosis (sealants). Optimal 
      patient selection is key to successful patient outcomes. This review discusses 
      bronchoscopic approaches for emphysema treatment which has progressed through 
      clinical trials to clinical practice.
