TI  - Exercise simultaneously increases nasal patency and bronchial obstruction in 
      asthmatic children.
PG  - 1493-1495
LID - 10.1111/resp.12849 [doi]
AB  - We found that simultaneous post-exercise increase in nasal patency and bronchial 
      obstruction occurs only in children with atopic asthma, but not in sensitized 
      children without asthma. In healthy children, the increase in nasal patency is 
      accompanied by bronchial dilatation.
