TI  - How many steps are enough to avoid severe physical inactivity in patients with 
      chronic obstructive pulmonary disease?
PG  - 1026-7
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2012.02207.x [doi]
AB  - While prognostically valuable, physical activity monitoring is not routinely 
      performed for patients with COPD. We aimed to determine the number of daily steps 
      associated with severe physical inactivity (physical activity level <1.40) in 
      this population. We found that a daily step value <4580 is associated with severe 
      physical inactivity. Our results are of significant value for clinicians 
      counselling patients with COPD to help avoid the morbidity of severe physical 
      inactivity.
