TI  - An unusual presentation of Castleman's disease.
PG  - 1012-4
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2010.01805.x [doi]
AB  - Castleman's disease is one of the heterogeneous group of lymphoproliferative 
      disorders of unknown aetiology. It commonly presents as a mediastinal mass. It 
      can be unicentric involving only a single site, or multicentric involving 
      multiple sites. We report a patient with unicentric Castleman's disease, in which 
      the mass was located in the posterior mediastinum and accompanied by a massive 
      pleural effusion, which is extremely rare in unicentric disease. This case report 
      highlights the imaging techniques used in the differential diagnosis and surgical 
      considerations due to the hypervascular nature of the tumour.
