TI  - Adult community-acquired pneumonia caused by macrolide resistant Mycoplasma 
      pneumoniae.
PG  - 1206-8
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2009.01619.x [doi]
AB  - A 28-year-old woman with community-acquired pneumonia was treated with 
      sulbactam/ampicillin and clarithromycin, but failed to show any improvement after 
      4 days. The antibiotic regimen was changed to pazufloxacin and rapid clinical 
      improvement was seen. Mycoplasma pneumoniae was identified as the causative 
      agent, and adenine (A) to guanine (G) mutation at position 2063 in domain V of 
      the 23S rRNA was noted in the isolate. The minimum inhibitory concentration of 
      macrolide antibiotics, including clarithromycin, of this isolate was greatly 
      elevated.
