TI  - Omalizumab (Xolair) in patients with steroid-resistant asthma: lessons to be 
      learnt.
PG  - S29-34; discussion S45-7
AB  - Very severe asthma and local pulmonary steroid resistance causes major problems 
      for patients, physicians and the health system at large. It usually results in 
      multiple admissions to hospital and high morbidity. Omalizumab was used to treat 
      such patients with success. However, in doing so, it raised a number of issues 
      relating to the best methods of using this treatment in such patients.
