TI  - Middle mediastinal thymoma.
PG  - 934-6
AB  - Thymoma is a common primary neoplasm of the anterior mediastinum. However, it can 
      also arise in other locations, including the neck, the posterior mediastinum, the 
      lung, base of the skull and the pleural cavity. There are only three previous 
      case reports of thymoma located in the middle mediastinum. This report describes 
      a patient together with a review of the literature on middle mediastinal thymoma.
