TI  - Peripheral T-cell lymphoma with diffuse pulmonary infiltration and an increase in 
      serum KL-6 level.
PG  - 452-4
AB  - Peripheral T-cell lymphoma is a subtype of non-Hodgkin's lymphoma. A case of 
      peripheral T-cell lymphoma showing diffuse pulmonary involvement together with a 
      marked increase in the level of serum KL-6 is presented. CXR and CT revealed 
      reticular and ground-glass opacities, which mimicked interstitial pneumonia. 
      Immunopathological findings and an analysis of T-cell receptor gene 
      rearrangements of the lung biopsy specimen led to a definite diagnosis of 
      peripheral T-cell lymphoma. In addition, the extensive proliferation of type II 
      pneumocytes, which stained strongly positive for anti-KL-6 antibody suggested 
      that the pneumocytes were the source of serum KL-6.
