TI  - Pulmonary blastoma within bronchioloalveolar cell carcinoma.
PG  - 339-42
AB  - Pulmonary blastoma is a rare tumour of the lung composed of epithelial and 
      mesenchymal elements that morphologically resemble the embryonal structure of the 
      lung. The authors report a 79-year-old man who was diagnosed with a pulmonary 
      blastoma within bronchioloalveolar cell carcinoma. Macroscopic, histopathological 
      and immunohistochemical findings suggested that the pulmonary blastoma was 
      closely associated with the bronchioloalveolar cell carcinoma.
