TI  - Microscopic polyangiitis with unusual lung involvement.
PG  - 678-81
AB  - Microscopic polyangiitis (MPA) is a non-granulomatous, systemic and small vessel 
      vasculitis accompanied by segmental necrotizing glomerulonephritis with no 
      evidence of other small vessel disease. We report a patient with weakness, fever, 
      and arthralgia whose CXR and thoracic CT showed widespread nodular infiltration. 
      His proteinase-3 anti-neutrophilic cytoplasmic antibody (c-ANCA) was positive. 
      The serum creatinine was increased and haematuria subsequently developed. Renal 
      biopsy revealed a focal segmental necrotizing glomerulonephritis which was 
      compatible with MPA. He was treated with high-dose corticosteroid and 
      cyclophosphamide. Because of a worsening CXR and hypoxaemia, mechanical 
      ventilation was applied. Despite this he died of respiratory failure following 20 
      days of treatment. Nodular infiltration is an unusual radiological pattern in 
      patients with MPA and is the reason for this report.
