TI  - Severe acute respiratory syndrome (SARS) in Hong Kong.
PG  - 259-65
AB  - Severe acute respiratory syndrome (SARS) is a recently recognized and highly 
      contagious pneumonic illness, caused by a novel coronavirus. While developments 
      in diagnostic, clinical and other aspects of SARS research are well underway, 
      there is still great difficulty for frontline clinicians as validated rapid 
      diagnostic tests or effective treatment regimens are lacking. This article 
      attempts to summarize some of the recent developments in this newly recognized 
      condition from the Asia Pacific perspective.
