TI  - New Obstructive Sleep Apnoea Multi-Night Diagnostic Devices. Is a Single Night of 
      Measurement Now Considered Enough?
PG  - 669-671
LID - 10.1002/resp.70263 [doi]
AB  - –. The apnoea‐hypopnoea index (AHI) varies from night to night. –. Multi‐night 
      testing improves diagnostic accuracy. –. Emerging multi‐night diagnostic devices 
      offer practical advantages but require further validation. –. A single night AHI 
      should be interpreted as an estimate rather than a definitive value, alongside 
      clinical judgement.
