TI  - Breathing-related changes of respiratory resistance in vocal cord dysfunction.
PG  - 1134-6
LID - 10.1111/resp.12735 [doi]
AB  - Vocal cord dysfunction induced by exercise in children with uncontrolled asthma 
      was identified by laryngoscopy. The paradoxical adduction of the vocal cords was 
      also indicated by the breathing-related changes of the forced oscillation 
      respiratory resistance showing prominent increase during inspiration and a large 
      positive difference between inspiration and expiration. The breathing-related 
      changes of respiratory resistance offer thus a useful first-line technique to 
      diagnose vocal cord dysfunction.
