TI  - Incidence and outcome of lung involvement in IgG4-related autoimmune 
      pancreatitis.
PG  - 1142-4
LID - 10.1111/resp.12599 [doi]
AB  - We evaluated the incidence and outcome of lung involvement in 35 patients with 
      autoimmune pancreatitis (AIP). Our results indicate that lung involvement is 
      commonly observed in AIP (40%). In addition, corticosteroid treatment improved 
      the lung lesions and appeared to reduce the probability of relapse compared with 
      pancreatic lesions (0% vs 36%). This is the first report to assess the long-term 
      outcome of lung involvement in AIP (52 ± 33 months).
