TI  - Prevalence of oropharyngeal antibiotic-resistant flora among residents of aged 
      care facilities: a pilot study.
PG  - 1139-41
LID - 10.1111/resp.12545 [doi]
AB  - Residents in 11 long-term care facilities, and presenting to a single tertiary 
      hospital site, were sampled to estimate prevalence of oropharyngeal colonization 
      with resistant Gram-negative bacteria. From 124 residents, only one isolate 
      (0.8%; 95% confidence interval 0.0%, 4.4) was multi-resistant (an 
      extended-spectrum β-lactamase producing Escherichia coli) indicating that 
      different treatment recommendations for respiratory infections in this population 
      may not be justified.
