TI  - Chest computed tomography for the diagnosis of Mycoplasma pneumoniae infection.
PG  - 144-5
LID - 10.1111/resp.12218 [doi]
AB  - We analysed 53 cases of laboratory-confirmed Mycoplasma pneumoniae infection with 
      cough lasting ≥ 7 days and chest radiography showing no abnormal findings. 
      Twenty-two (41%) of those patients showed abnormal findings on chest 
      high-resolution computed tomography. In the daily clinical setting, for 
      assessment of acute cough, physicians should be aware that it is difficult to 
      confirm bronchiolitis or bronchopneumonia due to M. pneumoniae by chest 
      radiography.
