DP  - 2014 Jul
TI  - Cannabis smoking and respiratory health: consideration of the literature.
PG  - 655-62
LID - 10.1111/resp.12298 [doi]
AB  - The respiratory health effects from tobacco smoking are well described. Cannabis 
      smoke contains a similar profile of carcinogenic chemicals as tobacco smoke but 
      is inhaled more deeply. Although cannabis smoke is known to contain similar 
      harmful and carcinogenic substances to tobacco smoke, relatively little is 
      understood regarding the respiratory health effects from cannabis smoking. There 
      is a need to integrate research on cannabis and respiratory health effects so 
      that gaps in the literature can be identified and the more consistent findings 
      can be consolidated with the purpose of educating smokers and health service 
      providers. This review focuses on several aspects of respiratory health and 
      cannabis use (as well as concurrent cannabis and tobacco use) and provides an 
      update to (i) the pathophysiology; (ii) general respiratory health including 
      symptoms of chronic bronchitis; and (iii) lung cancer.
