TI  - Chronic cough management: dealing with a sensation of irritation in the throat.
PG  - 1278-9
LID - 10.1111/resp.12166 [doi]
AB  - Among the various types of laryngeal paraesthesia suffered by chronic cough 
      patients, we often encounter 'a sensation of irritation in the throat (SIT)'. Our 
      study indicated that capsaicin cough threshold was significantly (P < 0.05) lower 
      in the SIT-positive group (13.9 μmol/L) than in the SIT-negative group (49.6 
      μmol/L). The establishment of treatment strategies for SIT would be advantageous 
      for treating chronic cough patients suffering from this laryngeal sensation.
