TI  - Compliance with home non-invasive ventilation.
PG  - 735-6
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2012.02169.x [doi]
AB  - Home non-invasive ventilation (NIV) is being increasingly employed to treat 
      chronic hypercapnic respiratory failure. However, there is little data on 
      compliance with home NIV. Sixty-five patients, aged 72.6 ± 9.4 years, who were 
      using home NIV were administered a questionnaire on symptomatology and adverse 
      effects associated with home NIV. Mean daily use of home NIV was 7.3 ± 2.9 h/day, 
      and the median percentage of days on which home NIV was used for ≥4 h/day was 
      96.7%.
