TI  - Pulmonary sclerosing haemangioma mimicking lung cancer on PET scan.
PG  - 903-6
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2009.01559.x [doi]
AB  - Sclerosing haemangioma is an uncommon lung tumour that typically presents as a 
      solitary, peripheral pulmonary nodule in the lower lobe. Little is known of the 
      appearance of these tumours on FDG-PET scan. We report two patients with 
      sclerosing haemangioma with increased uptake on FDG-PET scan, which complicated 
      the preoperative work-up. Although the CT scan features of these two masses were 
      compatible with the differential diagnosis of sclerosing haemangioma, the central 
      location and increased uptake on FDG-PET scan raised the suspicion of malignancy. 
      We conclude that centrally located large sclerosing haemangiomas may be avid on 
      FDG-PET scan, and that familiarity with this false positive finding helps in the 
      diagnosis of a solitary pulmonary nodule.
