TI  - Primary pulmonary synovial sarcoma, a rare primary lung neoplasm: two case 
      reports and review of the current literature.
PG  - 748-50
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2008.01317.x [doi]
AB  - This report describes the clinical, histological and immunohistochemical features 
      of two patients with primary pulmonary synovial sarcoma in the context of the 
      literature. Chest pain, cough, haemoptysis and an enlarging pleural-based mass 
      are the main clinical manifestations. Diagnosis depends on identifying 
      epithelioid or spindle cells microscopically and on immunohistochemistry showing 
      positivity for cytokeratin and vimentin and epithelial membrane antigen stains. 
      Surgical excision is the main treatment approach.
