TI  - Pandemic planning: non-pharmaceutical interventions.
PG  - S44-8
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2008.01258.x [doi]
AB  - Ongoing concerns about the emergence of an influenza pandemic continue as the 
      number of avian and human infections with the H5N1 virus mount. Adequate amounts 
      of vaccine or anti-virals are unlikely to be available early on in a pandemic, 
      and the latter could become ineffective because of resistance. These factors have 
      focused attention on the use of non-pharmaceutical public health interventions to 
      inhibit human-to-human transmission.
