TI  - SARS: public health measures in Hong Kong.
PG  - S46-8
AB  - As there are no validated and rapid diagnostic tests nor specific treatment for 
      severe acute respiratory syndrome (SARS) at the initial stage of the outbreak, 
      public health measures are vital for the control of the disease. These included 
      an enhanced disease surveillance system, expanded laboratory diagnostic capacity, 
      heightened infection control in hospitals and residential institutions for the 
      elderly, intensive contact tracing coupled with medical surveillance at 
      designated medical centres, quarantine of close contacts by way of home 
      confinement, formation of multidisciplinary investigation and response teams, and 
      public education and communication. The above measures were implemented in many 
      countries during the outbreak. To prevent spread in the region and beyond, port 
      health measures targeted at both entry and exit health screenings were also 
      carried out together with regional and international liaison.
