VI  - 6
IP  - 4
DP  - 2001 Dec
TI  - Primary pulmonary botryomycosis: an important differential diagnosis for lung 
      cancer.
PG  - 347-50
AB  - This is the sixteenth reported case of pulmonary botryomycosis, an uncommon 
      suppurative bacterial infection of the lung. We describe the case of a 
      69-year-old man who presented with a chronic cough and intermittent haemoptysis 
      and on subsequent chest computed tomographic scan imaging was found to have a 
      right lower lobe mass. He underwent a right lower lobectomy for presumed lung 
      cancer. Histological analysis however revealed a bacterial aetiology. The past 
      literature is reviewed outlining the pathogenesis and difficulties of clinical 
      and radiological diagnosis. Primary pulmonary botryomycosis forms an important 
      curative differential diagnosis for lung cancer.
