TI  - Medical thoracoscopy: Survey of current practice-How successful are medical 
      thoracoscopists at predicting malignancy?
PG  - 958-60
LID - 10.1111/resp.12725 [doi]
AB  - Use of medical thoracoscopy by respiratory physicians is increasing. This survey 
      of experienced thoracoscopists was conducted to establish current practice of 
      medical thoracoscopy and physicians' opinion of theoretical cases using 20 video 
      clips. Results suggest an increasing trend towards day-case thoracoscopy but that 
      caution is required when making diagnosis on macroscopic appearance: malignant 
      and benign disease could only be differentiated in 59% of cases, and trapped lung 
      is difficult to predict at thoracoscopy.
