TI  - A rational approach to single, dual and triple therapy in COPD.
PG  - 581-9
LID - 10.1111/resp.12690 [doi]
AB  - The complexity of COPD treatment has increased over the last 5 years mainly 
      because of the proliferation of drugs and delivery devices. In this paper, we 
      will focus on currently available therapy used for maintaining patient well-being 
      rather than acute relief of symptoms. We propose a series of principles for 
      rational therapy, and following a review of how currently available treatments 
      perform in isolation and when compared with each other, we suggest an approach to 
      aid the rational selection of the most appropriate treatment based on current 
      evidence.
