TI  - Variable agreement among experts regarding Mycobacterium avium complex lung 
      disease.
PG  - 348-51
LID - 10.1111/resp.12440 [doi]
AB  - Data regarding many clinical aspects of pulmonary Mycobacterium avium complex 
      (pMAC) are lacking. Guidelines rely substantially upon expert opinion, integrated 
      through face-to-face meetings, variably weighting individual opinions. We 
      surveyed North American non-tuberculous mycobacteria experts regarding clinical 
      aspects of pMAC using Delphi methods. Nineteen of 26 invited experts (73%) 
      responded, with extensive variability. Convergence could not be reached for most 
      questions. Respondents described extensive uncertainty around specific issues. 
      Findings underscore urgent need for more research.
