TI  - Anomalous isolated segmental pulmonary vein dilatation detected by computerized 
      tomography of the chest.
PG  - 1212-4
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2009.01636.x [doi]
AB  - This report presents findings detected on computerized tomography of the chest in 
      three patients with dilatation of a segmental pulmonary vein and its branches. 
      Each patient had dilatation of an isolated segmental pulmonary vein and its 
      branches with a normal distribution, and no associated cardiovascular anomalies; 
      in two patients, ground glass opacity corresponding to the distribution of the 
      dilated pulmonary veins was observed. The CT features are consistent with a rare 
      subtype of congenital pulmonary varix.
