TI  - Early recurrence of Pneumocystis jiroveci pneumonia in two HIV-infected patients: 
      linking infection relapse and immune reconstitution syndrome.
PG  - 910-2
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2009.01583.x [doi]
AB  - This case report describes two HIV-positive patients with Pneumocystis jiroveci 
      pneumonia who relapsed within 1 week of starting secondary prophylaxis and 
      antiretroviral treatment. Diagnostic and therapeutic approaches as well as the 
      need to establish risk factors for infection recurrence or early immune 
      reconstitution syndrome are highlighted.
