TI  - Recurrent respiratory papillomatosis with pulmonary involvement: a case report 
      and review of the literature.
PG  - 137-40
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2008.01421.x [doi]
AB  - Recurrent respiratory papillomatosis (RRP) is a viral infection that usually 
      affects the upper airways. Although it can spread throughout the respiratory 
      tract, involvement of the lung parenchyma is quite rare. Radiographic images of 
      RRP with lung involvement have been mainly presented in case reports of 
      paediatric patients. We present the case of an adult patient with RRP and lung 
      involvement, and detail the serial radiographic manifestations. CT and 
      reconstructed images were obtained. The literature was also reviewed and 
      radiographic features of RRP with lung involvement are summarized.
