TI  - Lymphomatoid granulomatosis mimicking interstitial lung disease.
PG  - 1085-7
LID - 10.1111/j.1440-1843.2008.01351.x [doi]
AB  - Lymphoid granulomatosis is a rare form of pulmonary angiitis. This case report 
      presents a patient with lymphoid granulomatosis in whom the clinical 
      presentation, radiological features and the partial response to corticosteroid 
      therapy mimicked interstitial lung disease. Lymphoid granulomatosis was only 
      diagnosed at post-mortem examination. The range of reported clinical 
      presentations, diagnostic approaches and outcomes are described.
