TI  - Pulmonary lymphoma developed during long-term methotrexate therapy for psoriasis.
PG  - 774-6
AB  - Low dose weekly administration of methotrexate has been thought to be effective 
      for both rheumatoid arthritis (RA) and psoriasis. However, there is a possibility 
      that methotrexate therapy may be oncogenic. This report presents a case of 
      pulmonary lymphoma developed during long-term methotrexate therapy for psoriasis. 
      Physicians should be aware that Epstein-Barr virus-associated lymphoproliferative 
      disorders that occur during treatment with methotrexate are not specific to 
      patients with RA.
