TI  - Strongyloides hyperinfection in a patient with sarcoidosis.
PG  - 105-6
AB  - A 51-year-old-woman presented with chronic eosinophilia, a diffuse interstitial 
      lung pattern on CT and splenomegaly with hypodense lesions. A diagnosis of 
      sarcoidosis was determined from a lung biopsy. Hyperinfection with strongyloides 
      following treatment with systemic steroids explains the presence of eosinophilia 
      and splenic involvement.
