TI  - Psittacosis with increased gammadelta T cells in bronchoalveolar lavage fluid.
PG  - 161-4
AB  - Experience with two cases of psittacosis is described here in which the number of 
      gammadelta T cell receptor-positive T lymphocytes (gammadelta T cell) in the 
      bronchoalveolar lavage fluid was markedly increased (25.1 and 66.9%) and CD8+ T 
      cells were also increased with reversal of the CD4/CD8 ratio. These values 
      improved to the normal range along with recovery of their radiographical 
      findings. The present findings suggest that gammadelta T cells may play an 
      important role in protection from lung injury caused by Chlamydia psittaci 
      infection.
