TI  - Pleural amyloidosis in a patient with intractable pleural effusion and multiple 
      myeloma.
PG  - 79-80
AB  - Pleural involvement of systemic amyloidosis has been rarely reported. We report a 
      case with multiple myeloma presenting an intractable right pleural effusion, in 
      which pleural amyloidosis was diagnosed through pleural biopsy using a Cope 
      needle. The diagnosis of pleural amyloidosis is important, because its refractory 
      pleural effusion should be treated with pleurodesis. Since closed pleural biopsy 
      using a Cope needle is much less invasive than thoracoscopy, the former should be 
      attempted first whenever pleural amyloidosis is suspected.
